# draw-on-turn (realms/docs/gear.md) at turn 2, one card: "At the beginning of your draw step, if it's your second turn,
# draw a card." Both players wear it. Bot1's second turn is turn 3, Bot2's turn 4 (CR 500.1: "your Nth turn" counts the
# turns that player has begun): each draws one more card in its own second draw step and in no other - not in its first or
# third (the intervening "if", CR 603.4), and not in the other player's draw step ("your draw step", CR 504.1). The
# maximum hand sizes keep the cleanup steps' discards out of the counts.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest x40

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x40

[Variant]
Bot1: maximum 20; emblem Gear test: draw-on-turn, turn 2, count 1
Bot2: maximum 20; emblem Gear test: draw-on-turn, turn 2, count 1

[Actions]
[T1 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 7
[T2 Bot2.Draw]
? Stack.Count = 0
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 8
[T3 Bot1.Draw]
? Stack = Gear test: draw-on-turn, turn 2, count 1
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 9
[T4 Bot2.Draw]
? Stack = Gear test: draw-on-turn, turn 2, count 1
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 9
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 10
[T5 Bot1.Draw]
? Stack.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 10
Bot2.Hand.Count = 10
